 "seat": {
  "BEST_WHY": "The floor masonry is the most convincingly made thing in the deck. The coursing runs in rows but the block lengths vary within a row (the row at y\u2248540 goes long-short-long-long across x 250\u2013650), and the damaged blocks \u2014 the dark ones at (405,400), (330,420), (560,395), (430,600) \u2014 sit *in* the coursing at block size rather than being splatted over it, so the floor reads as cut stone with individual failed pieces. The light falloff is smooth with no visible banding from the lit centre at (410,490) out to the dark floor at (100,700). The north wall band at y 200\u2013262 and the side wall columns at x 0\u201355 / x 690\u2013750 are cooler and smaller-coursed than the floor, so the wall plane separates from the floor plane without needing an outline. The stair/grate sprite at (183\u2013248, 455\u2013515) is still lit consistently with its neighbours (it goes darker with the falloff, unlike a pasted icon).",
  "WORST_WHY": "It is assembled, not made. There is no light source at all \u2014 the orc at (220,10) carries nothing and the frame is the same value edge to edge. The dirt floor from (55,0) to (245,195) is one speckle-noise tile stamped with zero variation; the grey wall at x 0\u201350 is identical courses with single-value mortar. The water pool at (248\u2013384, 0\u2013195) is a hard-edged rectangle against the dirt with no bank, no edge tile, no depth, and the three lily pads at (320,20), (325,115), (275,160) are one blob at three scales. Floor-to-wall boundaries at x\u224850 and y\u2248195 are hard lines with no contact shadow. The two barrels at (125,205) and (175,205) are the same sprite twice. The torch bracket at (30,135) has a flame that lights nothing. This is what a free tileset looks like when dropped onto a map with no pass afterwards.",
  "FLAGGED": "2, 3, 4",
  "RANK": "1 > 2 > 4 > 3",
  "BEST": "1",
  "WORST": "3",
  "SHIP": "NONE"
 },
