  "The crossed-timber props at (245,485) and (440,610) are chunky pixel sprites over sub-pixel painterly floor \u2014 same resolution mismatch as the figure. Match one to the other.",
  "A floor crack crosses onto a wall: the line that starts on the corridor floor around (545,250) continues through the wall at (565\u2013610, 340\u2013400). Cracks cannot pass from the floor plane to a wall plane. Clip the crack layer to the floor mask.",
  "The arc from (595,660) to (700,590) is one constant-width stroke over roughly eight blocks. Same fix as image 1: per-block, variable width, terminate at joints.",
